\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Corollary}
\title{A fixed selector admits inequivalent backgrounds}
\date{2026-11-08}

\p{Fix a \vocabk{selected Gaussian background}{fdip-005A}
#{b_0=(\Pi,w,m,P)} with a non-loop edge #{e_0}.
Take #{O=\{e_0\}}, or take the edge orbit of #{e_0} under a
fixed \vocabk{finite signed graph symmetry}{fdip-004S}.
Put
##{\begin{aligned}
I&=\left(-\min_{e\in O}w_e,\infty\right),\\
w_e^{(t)}&=w_e+t\mathbf1_O(e),\qquad t\in I,\\
b_t&=(\Pi,w^{(t)},m,P).
\end{aligned}}
Let #{Q_t} be the precision of #{b_t}. All weights are positive and the
\vocabk{raw selector map}{fdip-005E} is constant. In the orbit
case the given symmetry is preserved. The full
\vocabk{Gaussian induced action}{fdip-005R} strictly increases:
##{\frac{d}{dt}\mathcal W_{\mathrm{full}}(b_t)
 =\frac12\sum_{e\in O}\langle d_e,Q_t^{-1}d_e\rangle>0.}
Consequently distinct parameters give no directed or signed
\vocabk{background arrow}{fdip-005C}. On this family
#{\mathcal W_{\mathrm{full}}} cannot factor through
#{s_{\mathrm{sel}}}.}

\proof{
\p{The set #{O} is nonempty and consists of non-loop edges:
the signed endpoint condition preserves that property. In the orbit
case, adding the same weight to every edge preserves the original weight
invariance. A representation and idempotent supplying #{P} can
therefore stay fixed. In either case
##{Q_t=Q_0+t\sum_{e\in O}d_e\otimes d_e^\flat>0,}
because the weights stay positive and #{m>0}. The derivative is
\ref{fdip-005S} along this weight direction. Every summand is
nonnegative, and the one for #{e_0} is strictly positive since
#{d_{e_0}\ne0} and #{Q_t^{-1}>0}. The positive derivative on the
interval #{I} proves strict increase. Any background arrow would
orthogonally conjugate the precisions and hence preserve their
determinants, contradicting this increase. Finally, a function
of the constant raw selector data would be constant on the family.}
}

\p{This conclusion concerns the full action; it does not require
that every retained observable vary. Retained dependence is
explicit in the existing positive half-turn sector of
\ref{fdip-003S}: at fixed #{a=m^2>0} and for #{t>0}, its precision eigenvalues
are #{a} and #{a+2+2t}. Thus the selected law varies with #{t},
and the squared-norm expectation of \ref{fdip-005K} is
##{\trace_{V_+}C_P=\frac1a+\frac1{a+2+2t}.}
The projector remains fixed. In this family the
\vocabk{selected-structure map}{fdip-005E} #{\sigma}, which
includes the retained precision, varies along with the law.}
